# Drum and Dance  Launch on January 8th 2017

[![drum and dance launch](/media/2016/12/RC-Launch-141216-new-bleed-1-2.jpg)](/drum-dance-launch-january-8th-2017/rc-launch-141216-new-bleed-1/)   Rhythm Culture will be flying back into action on January 8th with our Drum and Dance Launch for 2017. This event is an introduction for all of the new classes that will be on offer in 2017. There will be loads of African drumming classes, a new DRUM SING DANCE for kids workshop, African dance workshops with LIVE DRUMMING and the long awaited Dundun drumming and Dundun dancing!! All of the classes require no experience and are open to all levels although they will still be fun and challenging for current students. Expect to have loads of fun, get a work out, meet new people and enjoy yourself immensely. Bring family, friends and give it a go. This is a great opportunity to try one of these classes before all of the courses and classes start for the year. Get all the specials online and come and celebrate the New Year with drumming and dancing! There will be no drum hire fee for this event and see below for the program.

